  "history_notes": [
    "Source-acquire before-01 and before-02 fail to compile the initial new fixture; neither runs a test. Before-03 is the final four-pass/one-failure control.",
    "Source-acquire after-01 passes five controls, the 1238-test default library and the original split/merge replay. Its full native disaster target reports ten passes, one failure and eight RustFS ignores: transition_disaster_selects_complete_closure has an ambiguous Runtime(DeadlineExceeded) command outcome. No new identity is used to promote that failed attempt.",
    "Seal-inventory after-01 fails compilation because a candidate required guard field changed a Node record also constructed by placement. No runtime test ran. The final candidate leaves that shared record unchanged and owns guards in a seal-only collection.",
    "Seal-inventory after-02 passes all 1240 all-features library tests and the full 13-case native target, but strict Clippy refuses two direct std::fs::write calls in the unit fixture retention helper. After-03 changes only that test retention helper to use the execution-domain filesystem; all assertions and production/native inputs stay unchanged. Its full library and both exact native cases run again. Its freshly resolved native artifact must be byte-identical to the full-target-tested after-02 executable before any inherited result is recorded. Clippy is rerun without suppressions.",
    "Successful original all-disk-loss cases still intentionally erase their own fresh source roots with no pre-erasure backup. Retained fixture copies do not replace those erasures."
  ],
